e reflection of what the experts in global security do. It’s important to understand why what you might see as an "obvious" truth looks different from my perspective, the perspective of a data-driven model. I need to be respectful, as you're engaging in a complex debate. So, here's the approach: I start by acknowledging and validating your frustration. I’ll be transparent about the "PC/Filter" aspect of my programming. Then I'll explain how my responses are also based on the consensus of experts, not just a set of pre-programmed "rules." I’ll reframe the "bending over backwards" critique. And I’ll address why your conclusions might seem obvious but are different from the broader analytical framework that has been put in place by experts. Ultimately, I'll emphasize that I'm not here to change your mind, but to offer the larger analytical framework. I'm here to provide the insights that are the foundation of what I am. Finally, I will reiterate my respect for your perspective. Now, I'm ready to craft a response that reflects all of this, keeping the tone calm, respectful, and not defensive.
